WEBVTT

00:02:58.864 --> 00:03:00.014
not just images.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.934
We were asked to help
a California district attorney

00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:06.379
understand prosecutorial delays
in their jurisdiction.

00:03:06.839 --> 00:03:09.506
There are people on probation
or sitting in jail,

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:12.141
awaiting for trial sometimes for years.

00:03:12.165 --> 00:03:14.609
They wanted to know
what kind of cases dragged on,

00:03:14.633 --> 00:03:17.757
and they had a massive data set
to explore to understand it,

00:03:17.781 --> 00:03:19.193
but didn't have the expertise

00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:21.765
or the instruments
in their office to do so.

00:03:21.789 --> 00:03:23.535
And that's where we came in.

00:03:23.559 --> 00:03:26.956
I worked with my colleague,
public policy professor Angela Hawken,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.466
and our team first created
a visual dashboard